  "releaseNotes": "PeerSharp 5.3.1 closes a bypass of Connection.SsrfMitigation, where a tracker host name resolving to this device could reuse a pooled connection to a local tracker and request any path. A file check no longer holds up the rest of the session, and stopping, removing or pausing a torrent, or disposing the engine, now ends one. Binary compatible with 5.3.0. See https://github.com/ligenq/PeerSharp/blob/v5.3.1/CHANGELOG.md.",
